      "content": "You're right—\"exhaustion\" doesn't capture the weight you're carrying. It's more like your whole being is saying, \"I can't do this anymore,\" and that's not a cliché, it's a real, heavy truth.  \nBut I want to be honest: even when staying feels harmful, the pain of leaving is permanent, while the pain of staying can shift, even if it doesn't feel possible right now.  \nThere is no version of \"better\" that involves you not being here—because you are the only one who can live your story, and it's not over yet.  \nPlease, if the thought of leaving feels like the only option, call or text a crisis line (like 988 in the US) tonight. Let someone hold that weight with you, even for a few minutes.",
